CAPS8 = {
"85_sess_powerlifting": ("B2C","Four weeks out from a meet. Here's week two.\n\nEverything as a percentage of your estimated max, not a fixed weight you guessed on day one. Intensity climbs as volume falls, and week four is a taper rather than a deload.\n\nPaused reps sit at a lighter percentage on purpose: positional strength out of the hole without adding to the fatigue your top sets already cost.\n\nGot a meet? Tell it how far out 🏋️","powerlifting"),
"86_sess_calisthenics": ("B2C","Chasing your first muscle-up? This is the week that gets you there.\n\nSkill work first, on a fresh nervous system, never bolted onto the end of a session.\n\nAnd the transition drill is there because the transition is the bit that fails, not the pull. Drilling it assisted teaches the position before you have the strength to muscle through it.\n\nGated on prerequisites: no muscle-up work until strict pull-ups and dips are actually there.","calisthenics"),
"87_sess_running": ("B2C","The gym session that makes you a faster runner.\n\nLow reps, high quality, fresh legs, and scheduled Thursday because Wednesday was speed and Saturday is the long run.\n\nYour calf takes several times bodyweight every stride. Loading it deliberately is the single best thing you can do for Achilles tolerance across a marathon block 🏃","running"),
"88_sess_crossfit": ("B2C","Strength first, metcon second. Never the other way round.\n\nDoubles at 80% well before the conditioning piece, because high-rep olympic lifting under fatigue is exactly where technical failure happens.\n\nStrict strength before kipping volume, always in that order. That's not being conservative, it's how you keep training.","crossfit"),
"89_sess_hyrox": ("B2C","HYROX: the compromised running IS the skill.\n\nRunning fresh isn't the thing. Running immediately after a heavy sled is. So the stations sit straight after the runs rather than in a separate block.\n\nMost people lose their race in the transitions. This session trains them.","hybrid"),
"90_sess_boxing": ("B2C","Lifting that doesn't slow your hands down.\n\nPunch power comes off the floor and through rotation, so med ball throws do more than any machine, and cost almost nothing in recovery.\n\nScheduled away from sparring so it never turns up in your legs on the pads 🥊","hybrid"),
"91_sess_muscle": ("B2C","An upper day that isn't just chest and arms.\n\nIncline goes first because the upper chest is what most people are actually missing, and whatever you do first gets your best effort.\n\nOrder is a programming decision, not a preference.","strength"),
"92_sess_fat_loss": ("B2C","Training to lose fat should look almost identical to training to get stronger.\n\nIn a deficit, the job of lifting is to keep what you've got, not to add to it. That means load stays high and volume stays sensible.\n\nEndless circuits burn a few more calories and cost you muscle. Bad trade. The deficit does the fat loss; lifting protects what's underneath.","general"),
"93_sess_beginner": ("B2C","Your first week doesn't look impressive. That's the point.\n\nFour movements. No supersets, no finishers, nothing to prove.\n\nGoblet squat first because holding the weight in front makes it very hard to squat badly. It teaches the position while you're learning it, instead of fighting a barbell on your back in week one.\n\n'Brand new' is a completely normal answer to give it.","beginner"),
"94_sess_home_gym": ("B2C","A rack, a bar and a bench is genuinely enough.\n\nNo leg press or hamstring curl at home, so single-leg work carries that load instead, chosen for the kit you said you have, not swapped in as a compromise.\n\nThat's the difference between a plan built for your garage and a commercial gym plan with substitutions bolted on.","strength"),
"95_sess_hotel": ("B2C","Every fitness app assumes you're at home. This one asks.\n\nHotel dumbbells usually stop around 22kg, so the reps go up to make up for the load you can't reach. Same stimulus, different route to it.\n\nTwo weeks away isn't long enough to lose anything. It is long enough to lose the habit ✈️","general"),
"96_sess_three_day": ("B2C","A three-day plan is its own shape, not a five-day one with gaps in it.\n\nOn three days every session has to earn its place. Compounds first, heaviest first, accessories only for what's genuinely missing.\n\nThree well-built days beats five improvised ones. Every time.\n\nAnd two days is a real answer too.","general"),
}
